<section class="section section-why">
  <header class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">00 / Why ChainShield</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Safety before the <em>signature</em></h2>
      <p class="section-lede">One wrong transaction can drain a wallet. ChainShield stops that.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="why-grid">
    <div class="why-card">
      <span class="why-num">01</span>
      <h3>Set your guardrails</h3>
      <p>Choose how much BOT you can send per transaction and per day, which addresses you trust, and which risky actions are never allowed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="why-card">
      <span class="why-num">02</span>
      <h3>Check before you sign</h3>
      <p>Paste any transaction — a transfer, an ERC-20 approval, a swap — and ChainShield tells you if it is safe, suspicious, or dangerous before it reaches the blockchain.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="why-card">
      <span class="why-num">03</span>
      <h3>Prove it on-chain</h3>
      <p>Every decision can be recorded on BOT Chain as a tamper-proof audit entry. If something ever goes wrong, you have a public, verifiable record that you ran a safety check.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="why-note">
    <strong>Why values are shown in BOT</strong>
    <p>Blockchains store amounts in the smallest unit, called “wei” (18 decimal places). It is like cents to a dollar, but with many more zeros. ChainShield lets you type normal BOT amounts and converts them automatically, so you never need to count zeros.</p>
  </div>
</section>
